## Develop

```console
go mod tidy
go build ./...
go test ./...
```

Write the logic of each stage in its `*_stage.go` file. `plugin.go` registers the
stages and wires them to the executors. The [Creating a Plugin]({{.TutorialURL}})
tutorial builds a plugin step by step.

## Run it with piped

Build the binary and register it in the piped config:

```console
go build -o {{.Name}} .
```

```yaml
apiVersion: pipecd.dev/v1beta1
kind: Piped
spec:
  plugins:
    - name: {{quote .Name}}
      port: 7100 # any unused port
      url: file:///path/to/{{.Name}}
```

Piped accepts `file`, `https` and `oci` URLs for `url`.

Then add the stage to the pipeline of an application, next to the stages of the
plugin that deploys it (the Kubernetes plugin in this example):

```yaml
pipeline:
  stages:
    - name: K8S_SYNC
    - name: {{quote (index .Stages 0).Name}}
```

Stage names must be unique across all the plugins registered in a piped. Piped
keeps one plugin per stage name, so a clash silently routes the stage to only
one of them.
